60	 * This page's dominant defect is a field that saves, flashes a green "Saved.", and
61	 * changes nothing — the pre-launch audit counted ~18 of them. Two turned out to be
62	 * genuinely dangerous once someone looked: the auto-suspend kill switch (an operator
63	 * disabled suspensions during an incident, saw "Saved.", and watched the sweep take
64	 * customer VMs offline anyway) and the domain markup (panel showed 0% while every
65	 * customer was billed a hardcoded 25%).
66	 *
67	 * So until a key has a real consumer, say so on the control itself. An operator who
68	 * is told a knob is inert loses nothing; one who believes an inert knob works makes
69	 * decisions on it. Amber, and `text-amber-400` specifically, because that is the
70	 * "attention, not failure" tone already used elsewhere in admin
71	 * (components/admin/EmailTemplateEditor.tsx:303) — no new visual vocabulary.
72	 *
